## Key Learning

Recovery Mode is an effective method for repairing Linux systems when critical operating system files have been accidentally deleted. 
When Internet connectivity is unavailable in the recovery environment, manually restoring essential binaries and libraries can provide a minimal 
bootable system. Once normal boot is restored, missing packages and kernel modules can be reinstalled, followed by validation of networking and 
application services to ensure the server returns to a stable production state.
